module Cell
// Cell::New(value), Cell::Get(cell) and Cell::Set(cell, value) are called like
// functions from this module, but the compiler provides them: importing this
// module is what makes them and the Cell<T> type available.
//
// A cell is a box whose contents can change. The binding that names it never
// changes; Cell::Set replaces what the box holds and evaluates to the new value,
// and every name, closure, array or record holding the same cell sees it.
// A cell that reaches another worker is copied, with a CellCrossesWorker warning.
